This solution has a time complexity of $$$O(n)$$$ and a space complexity of $$$O(1)$$$. It uses a sliding window approach to find the subarray with the most distinct elements.
For each element $$$a_i$$$ in the input array, it checks if it is the first occurrence of that element in the subarray. If it is, the right index $$$r$$$ is set to the current index. Similarly, it checks if the element is the last occurrence of that element in the subarray. If it is, the left index $$$l$$$ is set to the current index. The subarray with the longest length of distinct elements is the desired solution.

